# Project architecture

## Feature layout

- Domain code lives in `src/features/<feature>/` (boot, title, game, menu, portfolio, shared).
- Each feature exposes its public API via `index.ts`.
- Cross-cutting infra (i18n, data, hooks, shadcn UI) lives in `src/features/shared/`.

## File naming

- **Files:** kebab-case (`boot-screen.tsx`, `portfolio-game.tsx`, `experience-content.tsx`).
- **Exports:** PascalCase (`BootScreen`, `PortfolioGame`, `ExperienceContent`).
- Do not use PascalCase filenames for components (legacy `BootScreen.tsx` was renamed).

## Screen + subcomponents

Complex screens use a nested `components/` folder:

```
game-screen/
├── game-screen.tsx          # orchestrator
└── components/
    ├── game-footer.tsx      # one export per file
    └── konami-modal.tsx
```

Extract reusable or non-trivial React components to sibling files under `components/` (see `skill-bar.tsx`, `tech-icon.tsx`). Keep screen files as thin orchestrators.

## Cursor skills

- Personal Agent Skills go in `~/.cursor/skills/`, not in this repo.
- `.agents/` is gitignored; do not add skills to the project.
